steveyo scribed thusly:
>Hey - let's hear some details about tourney ascensions.  What's taking so
>long?

My tournament goal has been to ascend a Tourist. Last year I had to
walk out with the PYEC on Nov 30, this year I had the Amulet and was
looting my stash pre-Planes on the 22nd. As usual, finding an early
piece of my kit (speed boots) made all the difference. This was my
first time having everything I needed at the Castle, so I could go
wishless. Thanks to all for the recent discussion re: Free Action, I
wore it throughout and felt rewarded everytime I saw that I only
"momentarily stiffened" during the more nasty battles. Thanks to
another recent post, I also carried a camera with me to Astral for the
first time. In the past I only used them in the earlier goings,
assuming that the more powerful beings would probably enjoy having
their picture taken as they killed me, as it would make a lovely
souvenir for their wall. To my pleasant suprise, Famine was, however,
quite put off by my Tourist's holiday snap.

Feeling ascendable on the 22nd allowed me time to try the "Unknown
Challenge". I found KOL to be tedious at first, but I'm enjoying it
now. Being restricted in adventures per day meant that I barely managed
to defeat THAT Wizard of Yendor in time (on the 29th), but there was no
way to go on as the Dungeons of Doom won't open up for me for awhile
yet. Thanks to Robin for a very entertaining side diversion into KOL, I
plan to keep playing over there.



